            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 6 changed paths in full. This is a pure domain package that reads no files and runs no git; the changes add name validation, decode and encode helpers, a handoff builder and a correction predicate.",
              "CheckResultName in engine/review/names.go requires a 12-character lowercase hex head, a canonical number and the .json suffix. A name with a path separator, traversal segment or newline is therefore refused, and VerdictName and ResultOfVerdict apply the same check. The tests in engine/review/verdict_test.go cover those cases, so no path injection is reachable through these functions.",
              "DecodeResult in engine/review/stored.go uses strict decoding and duplicate-key checks, and it refuses an unknown member, a wrong version and a missing or null reply. MaxStoredBytes bounds the size that callers read, so there is no unsafe input handling or unbounded read introduced here.",
              "EncodeVerdict validates the JSON with json.Valid before it indents, so malformed input is refused with ErrReplyNotJSON.",
              "VerifiedHandoff in engine/review/handoff.go leaves ToRole empty for the Unverified outcome, which the parent record parser refuses. A review that has not been verified therefore cannot be treated as clear, and the test verifies this.",
              "No secrets, new dependencies or authorization surfaces are introduced."
            ]
          }
        }
