            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "CheckResultName, VerdictName and ResultOfVerdict refuse path-shaped, uppercase, short, long, zero-padded and wrong-suffix names. The tests in engine/review/verdict_test.go exercise those cases and the round trip between result and verdict names.",
              "NextNumber already matched on the head12-n prefix followed by a dot, so a .verifier.json file counts toward the next number. TestNextNumberCountsAVerdictBesideItsResult covers this.",
              "DecodeResult rejects invalid input: duplicate keys, unknown members, wrong or missing version, and a missing or null reply. TestDecodeResultRefusesWhatEncodeResultDoesNotWrite covers these, and a round-trip test covers the valid case.",
              "VerifiedHandoff sets to_role for Blocks and Clear and leaves it empty for Unverified. The test runs the filled record through roles.ParseRoleHandoff to check that an empty to_role is refused and a set one is accepted.",
              "IsCorrection and EncodeVerdict behave as documented and are covered by table tests. EncodeVerdict refuses non-JSON replies and keeps characters such as \u003c and \u0026 unescaped.",
              "I found no regressions on baseline behavior and no unproved candidate behavior. Behavior that depends on code outside the patch (canonicalNumber, jsonstrict, Handoff's default to_role) cannot be verified here, and I treat it as unchanged by this candidate."
            ]
          }
